[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573211581","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101176#issuecomment-2573211581","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101176","id":2573211581,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZYBe9","user":{"login":"arkology","id":43543909,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQzOTA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43543909?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology","html_url":"https://github.com/arkology","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-06T14:20:50Z","updated_at":"2025-01-06T14:20:50Z","body":"`INSTANCE_ID`  and `INSTANCE_CUSTOM` are used for (multi)meshes. In 3D you are using `BoxMesh`. They have such data. In 2D you are using `Sprite2D` and they don't have such data. Most likely you need `MeshInstance2D` (for more detailed information it's recommended to ask in community channels).\nBut at a quick glance, this info (about `INSTANCE_ID`  and `INSTANCE_CUSTOM`) is not mentioned in the docs.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573211581/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573406221","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101176#issuecomment-2573406221","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101176","id":2573406221,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZYxAN","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-06T15:58:28Z","updated_at":"2025-01-06T15:58:28Z","body":"There are two things going on here:\n1. `INSTANCE_ID` and `INSTANCE_CUSTOM` only work with \"instanced rendering\" (i.e. MultiMesh)\n2.  In 3D, we have auto-batching so basically all MeshInstances are MultiMesh internally. In 2D, we have a a different form of batching that uses instanced rendering, but doesn't use MultiMesh (for Forward+ this is only in 4.4)\n\nTherefore, `INSTANCE_ID` and `INSTANCE_CUSTOM` are only non-zero in the following cases:\n1. When using MultiMesh\n2. When using MeshInstance3D\n3. in 4.3, when using 2D in the Compatibility renderer\n4. in 4.4 when using 2D with all renderers\n\nIn practice, you should only really rely on having it available when using MultiMesh as the fact that 2D batching uses instanced rendering is an implementation detail and not a guarantee made by our API. \n\nOur documentation be updated to stress that these are features of MultiMesh, and may not be available outside of that context","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573406221/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573670347","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101176#issuecomment-2573670347","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101176","id":2573670347,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZZxfL","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-06T18:25:28Z","updated_at":"2025-01-06T18:25:28Z","body":"> In practice, you should only really rely on having it available when using MultiMesh as the fact that 2D batching uses instanced rendering is an implementation detail and not a guarantee made by our API.\n\nFor MultiMesh, is `INSTANCE_ID` guaranteed to be in `0`..`instance_count - 1` range though? Aka couldn't it be also batched with something else affecting the `INSTANCE_ID`? 🤔 This should be stated clear in the docs too (if it's not done already).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573670347/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573936549","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101176#issuecomment-2573936549","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101176","id":2573936549,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Zayel","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-06T21:12:59Z","updated_at":"2025-01-06T21:12:59Z","body":"> > In practice, you should only really rely on having it available when using MultiMesh as the fact that 2D batching uses instanced rendering is an implementation detail and not a guarantee made by our API.\n> \n> For MultiMesh, is `INSTANCE_ID` guaranteed to be in `0`..`instance_count - 1` range though? Aka couldn't it be also batched with something else affecting the `INSTANCE_ID`? 🤔 This should be stated clear in the docs too (if it's not done already).\n\nYes, its guaranteed to be in the `0`..`instance_count - 1` range. We don't batch MultiMeshes either in 3D or in 2D\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573936549/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]